{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the families of Menasheh son of Yosef.</b> Scripture elaborated the lineage of these daughters back to Yosef because he cherished the Land, as it is said (Exodus 13): ״והעליתם את עצמותי״ — 'and you shall bring up my bones' — and his daughters too cherish the Land. And to teach you that all of them were worthy: whenever a person's deeds and his ancestors' deeds are left unstated, yet Scripture specifies one of them and traces his lineage for praise, he is a righteous man son of a righteous man; and if it traces him for disgrace, in the manner of what is written (II Kings 25): ״בא ישמעאל בן נתניה בן אלישמע מזרע המלוכה״ — 'Ishmael son of Nethaniah son of Elishama, of the royal seed' — it is certain that all those mentioned with him were wicked."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:21.944979530Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}